# API, Service, and Repository

- New data flows must follow the existing three-layer structure: `*.api.ts` → `*.service.ts` → `*Repository.ts` (see the events and promotions features for concrete examples).
- UI code (components, pages, hooks) should talk to `*.api.ts` functions only – never directly to repositories or raw storage.
- Put business rules and orchestration in `*.service.ts` files; repositories are for persistence details only (localStorage, future HTTP, etc.).
- Use the existing `StorageService` abstraction for anything touching localStorage; do not reach for `window.localStorage` directly.
- Keep API modules as the public surface of a feature – if you feel tempted to import a repository or service directly from a component, add an API function instead.
- When adding a new feature, mirror the existing events/settings API structure instead of improvising a one-off pattern.
